        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                "word": "chaînette",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "dce43aca-3913-4b9b-b8e0-774c51fb79d1",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chaînettes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c367e471-d956-3dc6-8dcc-864a62401950",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petite chaîne."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "043557bb-d17d-4e90-b61c-35499329297e",
                                "sense_id": "c367e471-d956-3dc6-8dcc-864a62401950",
                                "text": "[…] ; le médaillon de lapis-lazuli, attaché par une chaînette d’or à son poignet, de temps à autre sonnait contre son assiette."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c97ea3c-d159-4899-a909-001d2d9aa018",
                                "sense_id": "c367e471-d956-3dc6-8dcc-864a62401950",
                                "text": "Hélène, avec la patience mélancolique des malades, s'amusait à entortiller autour de ses doigts une chaînette d'argent qui lui servait de bracelet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0225b293-1890-3ef5-8865-5a00edab34dd",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sorte de voûte dont le cintre est semblable à la courbe d’une chaîne suspendue par les deux extrémités."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a2db508-f608-4f10-9e4d-abae3a5f7695",
                                "sense_id": "0225b293-1890-3ef5-8865-5a00edab34dd",
                                "text": "Et, sous les arceaux, entre les massifs, çà et là, des chaînettes de fer soutenaient des corbeilles, dans lesquelles s’étalaient des Orchidées."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e12c9a0-771e-3c9a-a970-6c5f4bbc925e",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Courbe plane, qui correspond à la forme que prend un câble lorsqu'il est suspendu par ses extrémités et soumis à son propre poids."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94da6aae-df76-3828-a24d-9b725535438a",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "La partie du harnais des chevaux de carrosse qui sert à soutenir le timon et à le reculer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Élevage"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "580e0c79-93ef-38d3-8708-606424b319a3",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gouttière au bas d'un tympan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Imprimerie"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "824c819c-ab0c-3d44-830d-89c768116bb4",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Troupe de soldats rangés en cercle et garantissant ceux qui sont chargés de fourrager."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c21206ec-24db-3d2a-8c00-ad47373d86e9",
                        "entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Accessoire, appelé aussi tricotin, permettant de tricoter un tube de laine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6d2db4d-653f-436f-86f1-1f104a1b0ffd",
                                "sense_id": "c21206ec-24db-3d2a-8c00-ad47373d86e9",
                                "text": "Il y avait l’époque de la chaînette comme il y avait celle des billes et de la marelle. Nous nous procurions une bobine dont le fil avait été utilisé. Nous plantions quatre petites pointes autour de l’orifice central et avec des bouts de laine et une épingle, nous nous appliquions à confectionner une chaînette régulière aux couleurs mélangées. Mais à quoi nous servait-elle ? A rien le plus souvent. C’était à qui assemblerait les tons les plus variés et ferait le plus long métrage. C'était une occupation pour l’adresse de la main et le plaisir de l’œil."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "275de17d-58b0-438e-a91e-874a28755ba3",
                                "sense_id": "c21206ec-24db-3d2a-8c00-ad47373d86e9",
                                "text": "Les soirs d’été sont voués aux rondes, c’est comme ça, cherchez pas à comprendre, de même que l’hiver est la saison des billes et le printemps celle de la chaînette qu’on fait dans une bobine avec quatre clous."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b2848daf-5ace-4cf7-bab4-1428debae65b",
                        "source_entry_id": "10674f55-6e7f-3e96-8a7f-f1df7cf99bd4",
                        "source_sense_description": "Courbe plane, qui correspond à la forme que prend un câble lorsqu'il est suspendu par ses extrémités et soumis à son propre poids.",
                        "target_lang_word": "catenary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catenary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "950d164a-8977-3c52-8dbe-9ba8acd2563f",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4c35e7-76c8-36a4-aecc-c91dded4eebd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to a chain; like a chain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bb734ae-f449-4786-8ae4-cdb7da180ff0",
                                                "sense_id": "950d164a-8977-3c52-8dbe-9ba8acd2563f",
                                                "text": "In Europe, the organizer was the hostess and her principle was catenary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eba5d35c-de4d-4033-80c8-3819dac16ee4",
                                                "sense_id": "950d164a-8977-3c52-8dbe-9ba8acd2563f",
                                                "text": "The structure of the model chosen was catenary, and only one nonlinearity was introduced, in that part of the model representing bone growth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2acee3e0-9ecb-3ba3-a158-ac288542a299",
                                        "entry_id": "9f4c35e7-76c8-36a4-aecc-c91dded4eebd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to a catena."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4db355e1-33bc-4915-b207-e6033566428b",
                                                "sense_id": "2acee3e0-9ecb-3ba3-a158-ac288542a299",
                                                "text": "The sequence of soils of a more or less catenary nature as seen on the Martin Estate is about as follows :"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "catenary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9dd8cc0-1ca9-3752-971c-c13030a9c78e",
                                        "entry_id": "8f61b958-6d2a-3648-876a-af1e03e25b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The curve described by a flexible chain or a rope if it is supported at each end and is acted upon by no other forces than a uniform gravitational force due to its own weight and variations involving additional and non-uniform forces. It is described by the hyperbolic cosine function."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f57ee7c-a5aa-322d-9a11-98349203532d",
                                        "entry_id": "8f61b958-6d2a-3648-876a-af1e03e25b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any physical cable, rope, chain, or other weight-supporting structure taking such geometric shape, as a suspension cable for a bridge or a power-transmission line or an arch for a bridge or roof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d361f13f-9fa4-33f2-b34b-ee5a0b16d337",
                                        "entry_id": "8f61b958-6d2a-3648-876a-af1e03e25b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The curve of an anchor cable from the seabed to the vessel; it should be horizontal at the anchor so as to bury the flukes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                        "entry_id": "8f61b958-6d2a-3648-876a-af1e03e25b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cable, the segments of which between supports take a catenary geometric shape, supporting in turn an overhead conductor that provides trains, trams or trolley buses with electricity, or (metonymic) the combination of the conductor, the cable, and supports."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "215bf6de-a9be-41ba-a22b-b959f1ee533f",
                                                "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                                "text": "The result was catenary being torn down several hundred feet at a time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139658c3-a4b1-4b33-845f-0317e3654772",
                                                "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                                "text": "The colour-lights showed up much better than the semaphores which, in spite of their approach warning boards, are not readily visible at any distance between the supports for the catenaries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5f9f920-0a44-45b5-b8c4-81c8495766b2",
                                                "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                                "text": "The electric overhead was catenary, using 0000 contact wire, and the new railway employed the latest in electric block signal systems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fbefc3a-31a9-433f-863c-e49aa8a098dc",
                                                "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                                "text": "In addition the catenary itself is divided into 1-2 km sections (corresponding to mechanical sections or tension lengths) with motorized remotely controlled sectioning off-load isolators such that only one train is likely to be immobilized at any one time as a result of an incident associated with the catenary system."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c97953a-3bd5-4c0f-b35a-5610a1f1cea5",
                                                "sense_id": "326fefed-272e-3869-925b-4dc48f3d4e3c",
                                                "text": "Overhead construction was catenary rather than a single wire to allow the use of pantographs instead of trolley poles so that speeds could be higher."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
